<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Florentine Codex</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Florentine Codex is a sixteenth-century encyclopedic work on the Aztec world compiled by the Franciscan friar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernardino-de-sahagun">Bernardino de Sahagún</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahuas">Nahua</a> informants. Written in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahuatl">Nahuatl</a> and Spanish and richly illustrated, it is one of the most important sources on the society, religion and conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/florentine-codex.jpg" alt="Florentine Codex" width="320" height="353" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernardino de Sahagún · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Codex_florentino_51_9.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
